timeline.body:
In the old docs, this is https://www.elastic.co/guide/en/elasticsearch/reference/current/cluster-allocation-explain.html#_no_valid_shard_copy.  We could point to the API docs and include the example there, but there wouldn't be an anchor for a specific example in that system. Since it seems like something that we want to provide more explanations / context for, maybe a better home would be https://docs-v3-preview.elastic.dev/elastic/docs-content/tree/main/troubleshoot/elasticsearch/diagnose-unassigned-shards
@marciw I see a comment in https://github.com/elastic/docs-content/blob/main/troubleshoot/elasticsearch/diagnose-unassigned-shards.md that that info might be moved around still. WDYT?

> ALLOCATION_EXPLAIN_NO_COPIES

